id: undying-determination
name: Undying Determination
talentCategory: threshold
prerequisites: Tier of Power 4+, 3+ Threshold Talents
description: >
  Refusing to go down without a fight, you exhibit a final burst of power when you reach the end of your rope.
text: >
  Undying Determination: Refusing to go down without a fight, you exhibit a final burst of power when you reach the end of your rope.
  –Prerequisites: Tier of Power 4+, 3+ Threshold Talents
  (1)-[Triggered, 1/Encounter]: While below the Injured Health Threshold, if you receive Damage from an Attacking Maneuver that exceeds your remaining Life Points, halve that Damage.
  (2)-[Triggered/Defeated]: Set your Life Points to 1 higher than their minimum value. Then, until the end of your next turn, your Life Points cannot be reduced below that value and you may ignore all Health Threshold penalties.
  (3)-[Automatic]: If you trigger the second effect of Undying Determination, at the end of your next turn, your Life Points are reduced to their lowest possible value and you are Defeated.

---

# (1) Below Injured - Injured or Critical - an attack's Damage past your Life Points, once it is worked out (the `overkill-damage`
# Moment): asked of whoever plays you, halved, rounded down (chat.mjs overkillAnswer).
[triggered/overkill-damage, 1/encounter, chosen, effect 1]
requires belowThreshold("injured");
allow damage.halvedOverkill;

# (2) Ticked on the Defeated card - a Triggered/Defeated effect, the Keyword's one of the Encounter: your Life Points 1 above their
# least, held there - nothing takes them lower - and no Health Threshold penalties, till the end of your next turn (Undying
# Determination, a mark; chat.mjs undyingDetermination).
# (3) That turn ended: your Life Points to their least, and Defeated (the mark's own end).
[triggered/defeated, effect 2]
undyingDetermination();
